  "body": "From the third read of PR #3471 (comment 7081508525 on that PR). The two items do not block that PR. They are readings of the code, not results of a run.\n\n1. The CL text writer (`crates/cl/src/cl/text.rs:105`, `to_text`) has no rule for an arc whose ends round to the same micrometre. `camcraft-post` accepts a `.cl` dump as input. So a sub-micrometre arc in a `.cl` dump that is posted with the CLI is still read as a full turn. Today only tests and one `camcraft-motion` path (facing, with no arcs) write `.cl` text. Necessary work: give `to_text` the same rule as the stream writer of PR #3471 (`crates/post/src/post/cnc_arc_lattice.rs`), from one shared function, with a test.\n2. A full turn that is written as ONE record, with float noise that puts its end a little ahead of its start, becomes a straight Z move (`cnc_arc_lattice.rs:51-60`, `arc_guard.rs:64`). By reading, no generator writes such a record: full turns are written as two halves (`entry.rs:96`, `trochoid_bore`, `thread_ride`), and `push_arc` writes exactly equal ends as a line. Necessary work: state this law in `docs/decisions/3442-coincident-arc-blocks.md` (\"a generator writes a full turn as two halves\") and pin it with a test over the generators that make full turns.\n\nRefs #3442\n",
